If `i` is out of bounds, `this->arrayZ[i]` reads an offset from out-of-bounds memory. But the sanitize should have checked that `i` is within bounds.

Wait, but the sanitize checks `num_lookups` entries. If `num_lookups` is computed incorrectly (e.g., too small), then `subs[markIndex]` could access an entry beyond the sanitized range.

